| 4f | RIGHT AFTER | the rite's heal list (operator, 2026-11-17: //"future operators with lots of faces will be grateful this serves as a bridge we burn behind us and a smoother operational flow in future big maintenance projects."//; the items at lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/rite-heal-list): the prompts and passphrases (a face switch on an open vessel asking the route again, a keep lei offered to every face, a paper sheet printing before its refusal, the down and up a face with paper takes, cold-key cards left in scrollback, the wear under a pūlama, a mistyped pūlama route reading as none given); `up` blind to a stale vessel and its dirt warning; export and import (the pin budget against the wiki count, an empty wiki carrying nowhere, unregistered leftover folders, an import that leaves a standing row reading `already`, a minted wiki reading `document-unavailable` until held); the card, the guards and the census's two known red shapes (riding rank 13b). BUILT on `develop`: the pūlama route reading what it heard (`6d3d9b399`), the paper sheet refused before it prints (`5edfadc18`), parity's flags taking every path (`8fe52f79a`). Ruled 2026-11-18 (#/rulings): the repeated route and the wear under a pūlama heal by unlock and wear, every route prompt naming whose route it asks, and the keep lei offered to every face heals by one keep lei per house (backlog-awakens Wave 4). Holders: Lares-Awakens the runtime friction (backlog-awakens Wave 5: the paper-sheet dance, cold-key cards, holds against the wiki count, a minted wiki held at mint); Lares-Alpha the shim and the bundle (backlog-alpha #/next: `up` naming a stale vessel and its dirt warning, empty wikis travelling, leftover folders, `already` versus stood off, the keep's guards, the census's shapes with rank 13b) | The operator's house move met each of them on a real terminal, and every later big maintenance walks the same found, persona, unlock, export, import and keep doors. |

